luding the prior hosted Save timeout and five new asset tests. The large-asset test streams more than 25 MiB and verifies its complete digest. Final Wrangler deploy --dry-run passed with all four DO classes and both staging buckets (about 2.1 MiB uncompressed gateway bundle). Editor WASM and optimized native session were rebuilt; editor output reproduced the existing committed bytes and was staged for local testing.\n\nNo code was pushed or deployed, and no R2 assets or secrets were published in this checkpoint. Main is 14 commits ahead of origin/main after refreshing the remote reference, so a push would include this fix and the earlier Cloud Sync/recovery/target checkpoints. The user must explicitly request a push under the repository handoff rule.\n\nKeep this issue open. Remaining staging integration: publish the editor bundle to the asset bucket, configure GitHub/runner secrets, provide protected production runner HTTPS/WSS ingress to the NUC, then verify real GitHub authorization, provisioning, app previews and edge/hibernation behavior. Active GitHub webhook revocation, production desktop account attachment and cross-host restoration remain separate tracked work.","files":null}]}